// The Updates page. A .bin is uploaded with POST /upload (the session
// cookie and the X-CSRF-Token header, the file as the body), which answers
// {"uploadId": "..."}; or fetched from the configured mirror, then the
// release source. Either way its signature, channel and hash are verified
// before anything is unpacked.
//
// The same flow carries both targets: the base image (the OS, its slots
// and a reboot) and the product bundle (k0s, its images and the product,
// in their own slots on the state volume, with no reboot). The first
// product install is the same flow with no previous slot.

